*.log
npm-debug.log*

# Subagent-driven-development scratch workspace
.superpowers/

# Browser-test artefacts.
#
# Unanchored, and deliberately so. These read `packages/web/...` until #181 moved the tests,
# and the rename briefly un-ignored the old directory - which `git add -A` then swept 79 stale
# screenshots into. A rule pinned to a path stops covering anything the moment the path moves,
# and the failure is silent in the direction that matters: files start being tracked, not
# missed. Vitest also writes these beside each test file rather than only at the top of test/,
# so a plain `test/__screenshots__/` would miss `test/<area>/__screenshots__/` and a failure
# screenshot would arrive in a commit looking like a deliberate baseline.
.vitest-attachments/
**/__screenshots__/

# Written and removed by scripts/check-i18n.mjs; listed so a crashed run leaves no trap.
.lit-localize.check.json

# Screenshots and snapshots from the Playwright MCP browser, used for manual verification.
.playwright-mcp/
